HEAD(1)

NAME
     head - print the first lines of a file

SYNOPSIS
     head [-n count] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
     Prints the first ten lines, or the first count lines with -n.
     The quick way to see what a long file looks like.

EXAMPLES
     head /usr/adm/usage.log
     head -n 3 ledger

SEE ALSO
     tail(1), more(1)
